{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5143) to implement srd012-yes requirements R3.3, R4.1-R4.3 for the `cmd/yes` utility in the go-unix-utils project. The task is on branch `task/generation-run44-5143`. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.3: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully without printing error messages to stderr\n   - R4.1: Differential tests piping through \"head -n N\" comparing byte-for-byte via pkg/testutils\n   - R4.2: Test coverage for: no args, single arg, multi args, args after '--', empty string\n   - R4.3: Verify exit code behavior when stdout is closed early (SIGPIPE case)\n   - Task title also mentions \"version and help\" - adding --help/--version support\n   - AC6 requires cmd/yes to be feature-complete per srd012-yes\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/yes/main.go` and `cmd/yes/yes_test.go`. No git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary against GNU reference binary (gyes from Homebrew)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` and EPIPE detection\n   - Block-buffered output (8192 byte blocks) for high throughput\n   - `--` separator to pass arguments starting with `-`\n   - GNU yes only recognizes --help/--version when exactly one argument (argc==2)\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary`, `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`, `pkg/testutils.DiffTest`\n   - Custom `captureLines` approach needed because yes produces infinite output (can't use RunDiffTests directly)\n   - `errors.AsType[*exec.ExitError]` used in existing code (Go 1.23+ generics)\n   - Previous task (5142, commit cc2b7d88) implemented R2.1-R2.2, R3.1-R3.2\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd012-yes.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for all requirements R1-R4\n     - R3.3: \"Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully without printing an error message to stderr\"\n     - R4.1: Differential tests via head -n N, byte-for-byte comparison\n     - R4.2: Test cases enumerated (no args, single arg, multi args, --, empty string)\n     - R4.3: Exit code verification on SIGPIPE\n     - non_goals: \"does not implement any flags beyond --help and --version\" (implying those ARE in scope)\n\n   - `cmd/yes/main.go` — **ALREADY WRITTEN (updated)**\n     - Added --help and --version support via `handleSpecialFlag` (only when exactly 1 arg, matching GNU argc==2 behavior)\n     - Extracted `writeLoop` from main for clean structure\n     - Added `printHelp` and `printVersion` functions\n     - Added `fmt` import\n     - All existing functionality preserved (SIGPIPE handler, EPIPE check, block buffering, -- handling)\n     - Full updated code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"errors\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \t\"strings\"\n     \t\"syscall\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const blockSize = 8192\n     \n     func main() {\n     \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \n     \targs := os.Args[1:]\n     \tif handleSpecialFlag(args) {\n     \t\treturn\n     \t}\n     \n     \tline := buildOutputLine(args)\n     \tblock := fillBlock(line)\n     \twriteLoop(block)\n     }\n     \n     func handleSpecialFlag(args []string) bool {\n     \tif len(args) != 1 {\n     \t\treturn false\n     \t}\n     \tswitch args[0] {\n     \tcase \"--help\":\n     \t\tprintHelp()\n     \t\treturn true\n     \tcase \"--version\":\n     \t\tprintVersion()\n     \t\treturn true\n     \t}\n     \treturn false\n     }\n     \n     func printHelp() {\n     \tfmt.Print(\"Usage: yes [STRING]...\\n\" +\n     \t\t\"  or:  yes OPTION\\n\" +\n     \t\t\"Repeatedly output a line with all specified STRING(s), or 'y'.\\n\" +\n     \t\t\"\\n\" +\n     \t\t\"      --help     display this help and exit\\n\" +\n     \t\t\"      --version  output version information and exit\\n\")\n     }\n     \n     func printVersion() {\n     \tfmt.Println(\"yes (go-unix-utils)\")\n     }\n     \n     func buildOutputLine(args []string) string {\n     \tpositional := stripDashDash(args)\n     \tif len(positional) == 0 {\n     \t\treturn \"y\\n\"\n     \t}\n     \treturn strings.Join(positional, \" \") + \"\\n\"\n     }\n     \n     func stripDashDash(args []string) []string {\n     \tif len(args) > 0 && args[0] == \"--\" {\n     \t\treturn args[1:]\n     \t}\n     \treturn args\n     }\n     \n     func fillBlock(line string) []byte {\n     \tbuf := make([]byte, 0, blockSize+len(line))\n     \tfor len(buf)+len(line) <= blockSize {\n     \t\tbuf = append(buf, line...)\n     \t}\n     \tif len(buf) == 0 {\n     \t\tbuf = append(buf, line...)\n     \t}\n     \treturn buf\n     }\n     \n     func writeLoop(block []byte) {\n     \tfor {\n     \t\t_, err := os.Stdout.Write(block)\n     \t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\tif isEPIPE(err) {\n     \t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func isEPIPE(err error) bool {\n     \treturn errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/yes/yes_test.go` — **NOT YET UPDATED** (still has original code)\n     - Current state: has TestDiff (6 differential test cases), TestExitCodeOnSIGPIPE (non-differential, Go binary only), captureExitCode (no stderr capture), captureLines\n     - Planned changes:\n       1. Replace `captureExitCode` with `captureExitAndStderr` that also captures stderr via `cmd.Stderr = &stderrBuf`\n       2. Make `TestExitCodeOnSIGPIPE` differential (compare Go vs gyes exit codes) with table-driven cases: `{\"default\", nil}` and `{\"with-arg\", []string{\"hello\"}}`\n       3. Add stderr verification for R3.3 (`if len(goStderr) > 0 { t.Errorf(...) }`)\n       4. Use standard `errors.As(err, &exitErr)` pattern instead of `errors.AsType`\n       5. Keep existing `TestDiff` and `captureLines` unchanged\n     - Planned complete test file:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"bufio\"\n     \t\"bytes\"\n     \t\"context\"\n     \t\"errors\"\n     \t\"os/exec\"\n     \t\"testing\"\n     \t\"time\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n     \tt.Parallel()\n     \tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n     \trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gyes\")\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n     \t}\n     \n     \ttests := []struct {\n     \t\tname  string\n     \t\targs  []string\n     \t\tlines int\n     \t}{\n     \t\t{\"default-y\", nil, 5},\n     \t\t{\"single-arg\", []string{\"hello\"}, 5},\n     \t\t{\"multi-args\", []string{\"hello\", \"world\"}, 5},\n     \t\t{\"dash-dash-arg\", []string{\"--\", \"--help\"}, 3},\n     \t\t{\"dash-dash-only\", []string{\"--\"}, 3},\n     \t\t{\"empty-string\", []string{\"\"}, 3},\n     \t}\n     \n     \tfor _, tc := range tests {\n     \t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n     \t\t\tt.Parallel()\n     \t\t\tgoOut := captureLines(t, goBin, tc.args, tc.lines)\n     \t\t\trefOut := captureLines(t, refBin, tc.args, tc.lines)\n     \t\t\tif !bytes.Equal(goOut, refOut) {\n     \t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"output mismatch\\ngo:  %q\\nref: %q\", goOut, refOut)\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t})\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func TestExitCodeOnSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n     \tt.Parallel()\n     \tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n     \trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gyes\")\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n     \t}\n     \n     \tcases := []struct {\n     \t\tname string\n     \t\targs []string\n     \t}{\n     \t\t{\"default\", nil},\n     \t\t{\"with-arg\", []string{\"hello\"}},\n     \t}\n     \n     \tfor _, tc := range cases {\n     \t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n     \t\t\tt.Parallel()\n     \t\t\tgoCode, goStderr := captureExitAndStderr(t, goBin, tc.args)\n     \t\t\trefCode, _ := captureExitAndStderr(t, refBin, tc.args)\n     \t\t\tif goCode != refCode {\n     \t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"exit code mismatch: go=%d ref=%d\", goCode, refCode)\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tif len(goStderr) > 0 {\n     \t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected stderr on SIGPIPE: %q\", goStderr)\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t})\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func captureExitAndStderr(t *testing.T, binary string, args []string) (int, []byte) {\n     \tt.Helper()\n     \tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)\n     \tdefer cancel()\n     \n     \tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, binary, args...)\n     \tstdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Fatalf(\"StdoutPipe: %v\", err)\n     \t}\n     \tvar stderrBuf bytes.Buffer\n     \tcmd.Stderr = &stderrBuf\n     \tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Fatalf(\"Start: %v\", err)\n     \t}\n     \n     \tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(stdout)\n     \tif scanner.Scan() {\n     \t\t_ = scanner.Text()\n     \t}\n     \tstdout.Close()\n     \n     \terr = cmd.Wait()\n     \tif err == nil {\n     \t\treturn 0, stderrBuf.Bytes()\n     \t}\n     \tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n     \tif errors.As(err, &exitErr) {\n     \t\treturn exitErr.ExitCode(), stderrBuf.Bytes()\n     \t}\n     \tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected wait error: %v\", err)\n     \treturn -1, nil\n     }\n     \n     func captureLines(t *testing.T, binary string, args []string, n int) []byte {\n     \tt.Helper()\n     \tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)\n     \tdefer cancel()\n     \n     \tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, binary, args...)\n     \tstdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Fatalf(\"StdoutPipe: %v\", err)\n     \t}\n     \tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n     \t\tt.Fatalf(\"Start: %v\", err)\n     \t}\n     \n     \tvar buf bytes.Buffer\n     \tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(stdout)\n     \tfor i := 0; i < n && scanner.Scan(); i++ {\n     \t\tbuf.Write(scanner.Bytes())\n     \t\tbuf.WriteByte('\\n')\n     \t}\n     \n     \tstdout.Close()\n     \t_ = cmd.Wait()\n     \treturn buf.Bytes()\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. main.go was written successfully. Test file has not been written yet, so no build or test has been run.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Determined that R3.3, R4.1, R4.2 were largely already implemented by the previous task (5142)\n   - Key gap identified: R4.3's SIGPIPE exit code test was not differential (only tested Go binary, not compared against gyes)\n   - Decided to add --help/--version support because: (a) task title says \"version and help\", (b) SRD non_goals imply they're in scope, (c) without them `yes --help` would output \"--help\" infinitely instead of help text\n   - Determined GNU yes only handles --help/--version with exactly 1 argument (argc==2) based on C source analysis of `parse_long_options`\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The full stitch task description with all project context, SRDs, architecture, execution constitution, go style constitution, package contracts, shared protocols, task requirements, acceptance criteria, constraints, and design decisions.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write the updated `cmd/yes/yes_test.go` file (planned content is detailed above in section 3)\n   - Run `go build -o bin/yes ./cmd/yes/` to verify compilation (AC3)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/yes/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC4)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria AC1-AC6\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the middle of implementing task #5143. I had just successfully written the updated `cmd/yes/main.go` with --help/--version sup